.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1111 AM PDT Sat Oct 31 2026

Breezy onshore winds this afternoon with VFR ceilings. Winds ease
this evening ahead of the first few rainbands. Light rain showers
are forecast to arrive between 11 PM PDT - 1 AM PST (06-08Z).
Ceilings may lower as the rain approaches the coast, remaining
mainly VFR with a chance of borderline VFR-MVFR decks. Impacts to
visibility are also possible. Overall, medium confidence on rain
impacts as this morning`s 12Z KOAK sounding measured decreased
moisture content compared to yesterday with dry air confined to the
surface. Lower confidence on impacts at terminals in rain shadowed
areas, such as SJC and LVK. Dry, VFR conditions prevail through
Sunday morning with the potential for some lingering showers over
Monterey Bay.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR with high clouds cruising through. Onshore
winds increase this afternoon and ease in the evening. Moderate
confidence for light rain showers to arrive at the terminals around
midnight with lower VFR ceilings and slight visibility reductions.
If rain develops overnight, expect improved conditions by Sunday
morning with increasing moderate northwesterly breezes.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR as onshore winds increase this
afternoon. Winds ease and shift southerly as light rain showers
approach the terminals. If the rain materializes, borderline MVFR-
VFR ceilings and visibility reductions are possible overnight with
conditions improving by late Sunday morning.

